  "body": {
    "id": "prop:finite-margin-plugin-ranking",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "For a fixed finite family of valid cylinder identifying functionals \\(F_1,\\ldots,F_m\\), suppose each trajectory obeys the hypotheses of \\(\\mathrm{lem:valid\\text{-}cylinder\\text{-}hac\\text{-}delta}\\), and let \\(\\theta_j=F_j(p_{F_j})\\).  If \\(\\Delta=\\min_{j\\ne k}|\\theta_j-\\theta_k|>0\\), then the ordering induced by \\(\\widehat\\theta_{F_1},\\ldots,\\widehat\\theta_{F_m}\\) equals the population ordering with probability tending to one.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "A",
      "F",
      "pF",
      "theta",
      "thetahat",
      "T"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "lem:valid-cylinder-hac-delta"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "For every fixed \\(j\\), \\(\\mathrm{lem:valid\\text{-}cylinder\\text{-}hac\\text{-}delta}\\) gives \\(\\widehat\\theta_{F_j}\\to_p\\theta_j\\).  Since \\(m<\\infty\\), the union bound yields\n\\[\n P\\!\\left(\\max_{1\\le j\\le m}|\\widehat\\theta_{F_j}-\\theta_j|\\ge\\Delta/3\\right)\n \\le\\sum_{j=1}^mP\\!\\left(|\\widehat\\theta_{F_j}-\\theta_j|\\ge\\Delta/3\\right)\n \\longrightarrow0.\n\\]\nOn the complementary event, \\(\\theta_j<\\theta_k\\) implies\n\\[\n \\widehat\\theta_{F_j}<\\theta_j+\\Delta/3\n \\le\\theta_k-2\\Delta/3\n <\\widehat\\theta_{F_k}.\n\\]\nEvery pairwise comparison, and hence the full ranking, is then correct.",
